-- title:
--   Remark 4.16: Generated algebra and canonical Euler derivations
-- statement:
--   All vector spaces and Lie algebras are finite dimensional and real, with their usual Hausdorff topology. An invariant set is invariant under the group generated by $e^{\operatorname{ad}y}$. A closed convex set is pointed when its recession edge is zero. Write $\mathcal O_x=\operatorname{Inn}(\mathfrak g)x$, $\operatorname{co}(x)=\overline{\operatorname{conv}}\mathcal O_x$, and $C_x=\operatorname{cone}(\mathcal O_x)$. Admissibility means existence of a pointed generating invariant closed convex subset.
--
--   In the admissible structural setting assume $\mathfrak z=[V,V]$, let $h\in[\mathfrak l,\mathfrak l]$ be Euler, and choose an $\mathfrak l$-module splitting $V_h=A\oplus B$ for which $[A,A]$, $[B,B]$, and $[A,B]+[V_{h,0},V_{h,0}]$ have direct sum. Construct $D$ as in the preceding proof, with module corrections $+1/2,-1/2,0$ on $A,B,V_{h,0}$ and central weights $1,-1,0$ on these three bracket spaces. Write $\mathfrak g_D$ for the subalgebra generated by the $\pm1$ grades and $\mathfrak s_h$ for the ideal of $\mathfrak l$ generated by $h$. Then
--
--   $$\mathfrak g_0(D)=\mathfrak z_0(D)\oplus A_{-1/2}(h)\oplus B_{1/2}(h)\oplus V_{h,0}\oplus\mathfrak l_0(h),\quad\mathfrak g_D\cap\mathfrak l=\mathfrak s_h,$$
--   $$[\mathfrak l_{\pm1}(h),A_{\mp1/2}(h)]=A_{\pm1/2}(h),\quad\mathfrak g_D=\mathfrak g\iff\mathfrak s_h=\mathfrak l\text{ and }V_{h,0}=0.$$
--
--   If $\mathfrak s_h=\mathfrak l$, one may instead choose $D=D_{\rm can}+\operatorname{ad}h$, which is Euler and satisfies $\mathfrak g_0(D)=[\mathfrak g_1(D),\mathfrak g_{-1}(D)]$. All eigenspaces above are defined by their indicated operators and weights.
-- source:
--   Elements in pointed invariant cones in Lie algebras and corresponding affine pairs, arXiv:2110.07297v1, PDF p. 25, Remark 4.16: Generated algebra and canonical Euler derivations

